# local-failover-qwen27 — the default cloud→local failover tier AND, since
# 2026-08-11, the default interactive local brain. Two ways in:
#   1. Failover — the :8083 hybrid router picks it when this host is offline and
#      the failed-over session, AFTER bare-mode stripping, fits a 32K window.
#   2. Deliberate — `/model qwen` (MODEL_ROUTES) and the `qwen` wrapper's
#      default/lean mode (via :8082). Both are bare: the route path strips via
#      ROUTE_BARE below, and the wrapper's lean mode already passes --bare
#      client-side, so its prompt is ~945 tokens and 32K is generous.
#
# Two wrapper modes deliberately do NOT come here:
#   `qwen full` — full mode exists to carry the harness (~29K tokens), which
#     does not fit 32K with room left to converse, and stripping it server-side
#     would defeat the mode's whole purpose. Stays on the 4B @ 64K; see
#     local-qwen35.env and the 2026-07-09 prefill revert.
#   `qwen fast` — "fast" means fast. Stays on the 4B (local-fast.env); a 27B is
#     the opposite of what that flag asks for.
#
#   qwen3.8:27b-bare — GGUF, **17GB resident** on this 36GB M5 Max at
#   OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=2 (measured 2026-08-16, Ollama 0.32.13, and re-measured
#   under an 8K-token load without moving). That is 6GB LESS than the 3.5 tag it
#   replaces, despite 3.8 carrying an extra vision projector layer.
#   See modelfiles/bare/qwen3.8-27b-bare.Modelfile.
#   (Upgraded 2026-08-16 from qwen3.5:27b-bare. This line used to read "int4,
#   ~15GB"; both halves were wrong and the pair of them panicked this host —
#   int4 loads on the MLX engine, which ignores num_ctx, and 15GB was a lazily
#   allocated floor rather than a steady state. The Modelfile has the full
#   post-mortem. Do not restore an int4 tag here.)
#
#   The 3.5 → 3.8 jump skips 3.7 because Qwen never shipped one on Ollama; the
#   library goes 3.5 → 3.6 → 3.8. It also REQUIRED Ollama ≥ 0.32 — 0.23.4
#   refuses this tag with a zero-byte "please download the latest version" pull
#   that still exits 0. Rolling back to qwen3.6:27b needs no daemon change;
#   rolling back to 3.8 from a downgraded daemon does.
#
# Why a 27B here when the ladder spent a month on a 4B: the 2026-07-09 revert
# (9B → 4B) was a prefill-latency fix, not a memory fix — a 9B cold-prefilling a
# ~186K-token failed-over session ran ~5 min/turn and 500'd. Bare mode removes
# the reason those sessions were 186K tokens (system prompt + tool definitions +
# tool results + images), so the model can grow instead of shrink. Measured
# end-to-end through the router: 50,439 tokens → 1,196, answered in 3.6s.
# Keep these two changes together — reverting bare mode without also reverting
# this profile re-arms exactly that regression on a much larger model.
#
# TOOL-CAPABLE, and that is why it is qwen and not deepseek. This tier is paired
# with `failover_keep_tools=local`, which passes Read/Edit/Bash/Glob/Grep
# through so the model can keep doing work offline. deepseek-r1 cannot: Ollama
# rejects any request carrying tool definitions with HTTP 400 ("does not support
# tools"), which kills the session failover exists to save. If this tier is ever
# swapped for a model without tool support, set failover_keep_tools="" too.
#
# REASONING_EFFORT=none suppresses qwen3.8's thinking traces for latency.
# Verified 2026-08-06 on qwen3.5 that this does NOT break tool calling (both
# settings emitted a correct get_weather call).
#
# RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-16 on qwen3.8:27b-bare under Ollama 0.32.13, which changed
# the model AND the daemon at once. Tested on the /v1 path this profile actually
# uses: with reasoning_effort=none the model still emitted a correct get_weather
# call AND the `reasoning` field came back empty, so suppression works without
# costing tool use. Also passes on /api/chat.
#
# Test the /v1 path, not just /api/chat: `reasoning_effort` as a top-level
# /api/chat argument did NOT suppress thinking here, so checking only that
# endpoint would have reported a false failure. PROVIDER_BASE_URL below is /v1
# for a reason.
#
# Re-run after the next Ollama or model upgrade; a tier that stops calling tools
# fails quietly, and failover keeps looking healthy until the model has to
# actually do something:
#   curl -s localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"model":"qwen3.8:27b-bare","reasoning_effort":"none",
#          "messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Weather in Paris? Use the tool."}],
#          "tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_weather",
#            "parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"type":"string"}}}}}]}' \
#     | jq '.choices[0].message.tool_calls'
# A non-null tool_calls array is the pass condition.

PROVIDER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
PROVIDER_API_KEY=ollama
PROVIDER_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b-bare

# Strip the harness on an explicit `/model qwen` too, not just on failover.
# This tier is 32K by design (see the Modelfile), which only works because bare
# mode keeps the prompt small. A deliberate `/model qwen` hits MODEL_ROUTES and
# skips the failover branch, so without this it would arrive unstripped and
# overflow. See `route_bare` in src/proxy/config.py.
ROUTE_BARE=true

# Vendor sampling for qwen3.8 (matches the tag's own parameters).
PROVIDER_MAX_TOKENS=8192
PROVIDER_TEMPERATURE=1.0
PROVIDER_TOP_P=0.95
PROVIDER_REASONING_EFFORT=none

HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8082
LOG_FILE=proxy.log

SKIP_QUOTA_PROBES=true
SKIP_TITLE_GENERATION=true
SKIP_SUGGESTION_MODE=true
MOCK_PREFIX_DETECTION=true
MOCK_FILEPATH_EXTRACTION=true

CLAUDE_WORKSPACE=./workspace
MAX_CLI_SESSIONS=5

# Escalate off this tier instead of failing when a session outgrows its window.
# ROUTE_BARE above bounds the prompt, not the transcript, so a long-lived `qwen`
# session walks past 32K on its own. Matches this tier's FAILOVER_LADDER bound so
# a deliberate route and a failover size it identically; over it, the request
# goes to the 4B 256K tier. See route_max_input_tokens in src/proxy/config.py.
ROUTE_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=28000
